  "label": "Auschwitz Concentration Camp",
  "description": "Auschwitz was the largest and most infamous Nazi concentration and extermination camp, located in occupied Poland. It was the site of the mass murder of over 1.1 million people, mostly Jews, but also Poles, Roma, Soviet prisoners of war, and others. The camp symbolizes the Holocaust and the industrialized killing of millions. The meme's reference to 'Auschwitz' is a direct and offensive allusion to this site of genocide.",
